@zeroace074
Use this to store all item to a variable and remove the item from that storgae (if you don't want that, you can remove the line that removes the items.
JavaScript:
// Move all items form storage 0 to game variable 1
var storage = $gameStorageSystems.storage(0);
var items = [];
storage.allItems().forEach(function(item) {
    var amount = storage.numItems(item);
    storage.removeItem(item, amount);
    items.push({ item: item, amount: amount});
});
$gameVariables.setValue(1, items);
You can use this code to extract all items from such variable to a storage system.
JavaScript:
// Add all items stored in game variable 1 to storage 1
var items = $gameVariables.value(1);
if (items) {
    items.forEach(function(data) {
        $gameStorageSystems
          .storage(1)
          .addItem(data.item, data.amount);
    });
}
Change all IDs accordingly.

